Description: ABSP, which stands for "Analysis of Bisulfite Sequencing PCR", 
    is an R-based tool designed to analyze CpG methylation profiles using data 
    from Bisulfite Sequencing PCR (BSP) experiments. It was developed to assist 
    researchers in estimating and comparing methylation percentages of a DNA 
    region studied through BSP experiments. 
    ABSP offers a comprehensive automated workflow, spanning from trace file 
    sequencing results to data visualization and statistical analysis.
